@startuml
' ============================================================================
' METADATA
'   author:       TheRobotDrafts Examples
'   description:  Multi-region production deployment with global CDN edge,
'                 two regional stacks (LB + app tier + data tier), and a
'                 shared control plane.
'   usecase:      Globally distributed service requiring regional data
'                 residency, cross-region replication, and central control.
'   complexity:   complex
'   domain:       deployment
' ============================================================================
title Example Deployment Diagram - Complex Multi-Region Production

' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
' This diagram models a production system spanning MULTIPLE geographic
' regions plus a global edge and a central control plane. It demonstrates:
'
'   * `frame` blocks to GROUP nodes that belong to one region or one plane
'   * `cloud` for the global CDN / edge layer
'   * MIXED stereotypes: <<device>> for physical/virtual hosts,
'     <<executionEnvironment>> for the OS/runtime layer an app sits on
'   * Cross-region replication paths (a DB in region A talks to a DB in
'     region B) — long arrows that span frames
'   * Many artifacts: each tier runs several distinct software packages
'
' Layout tip: use `frame` to draw a labeled box around nodes that share a
' deployment boundary (a region, a VPC, a cluster). Frames make a big
' diagram readable.
' ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

' --- Global edge -----------------------------------------------------------
' The CDN sits in front of everything. Users hit the nearest edge POP.
cloud "Global CDN Edge" as cdn {
  artifact "Cloudflare\nWorkers" as edge <<deploy>>
  artifact "TLS\ntermination" as tls <<deploy>>
}

' --- Shared control plane -------------------------------------------------
' A single control plane that BOTH regions report to. It holds config,
' secrets, metrics aggregation, and CI/CD deployment state.
frame "Control Plane (us-east)" as cp {
  node "Config Server" as cfg <<device>> {
    artifact "Consul\n1.17" as consul <<deploy>>
    artifact "consul-agent" as cagent <<deploy>>
  }
  node "Metrics Aggregator" as metrics <<device>> {
    artifact "Prometheus\n2.50" as prom <<deploy>>
    artifact "Grafana\n11.0" as grafana <<deploy>>
  }
  database "CI/CD State Store" as cicd <<database>> {
    artifact "build-records.db" as builddb <<deploy>>
  }
}

' --- Region: us-east -------------------------------------------------------
frame "Region: us-east-1" as region1 {
  node "Edge LB (us-east)" as lb1 <<device>> {
    artifact "Ubuntu 22.04" as lb1os <<executionEnvironment>>
    artifact "HAProxy 2.8" as lb1haproxy <<deploy>>
  }
  node "App Host A1" as appA1 <<device>> {
    artifact "UML-IDE Backend\n2.0.0.jar" as appA1jar <<deploy>>
    artifact "Filebeat\n(log shipper)" as fbA1 <<deploy>>
  }
  node "App Host A2" as appA2 <<device>> {
    artifact "UML-IDE Backend\n2.0.0.jar" as appA2jar <<deploy>>
    artifact "Filebeat\n(log shipper)" as fbA2 <<deploy>>
  }
  database "Cache (us-east)" as cache1 <<database>> {
    artifact "redis-server\n7.2" as redis1 <<deploy>>
  }
  database "Postgres Primary (us-east)" as dbPrimary <<database>> {
    artifact "UML-IDE Schema\n2.0.0.sql" as schema1 <<deploy>>
  }
}

' --- Region: eu-west -------------------------------------------------------
frame "Region: eu-west-1" as region2 {
  node "Edge LB (eu-west)" as lb2 <<device>> {
    artifact "Ubuntu 22.04" as lb2os <<executionEnvironment>>
    artifact "HAProxy 2.8" as lb2haproxy <<deploy>>
  }
  node "App Host B1" as appB1 <<device>> {
    artifact "UML-IDE Backend\n2.0.0.jar" as appB1jar <<deploy>>
    artifact "Filebeat\n(log shipper)" as fbB1 <<deploy>>
  }
  node "App Host B2" as appB2 <<device>> {
    artifact "UML-IDE Backend\n2.0.0.jar" as appB2jar <<deploy>>
    artifact "Filebeat\n(log shipper)" as fbB2 <<deploy>>
  }
  database "Cache (eu-west)" as cache2 <<database>> {
    artifact "redis-server\n7.2" as redis2 <<deploy>>
  }
  database "Postgres Replica (eu-west)" as dbReplica <<database>> {
    artifact "UML-IDE Schema\n2.0.0.sql" as schema2 <<deploy>>
  }
}

' --- Traffic flow: user -> CDN -> regional LB -> app ----------------------
cloud "Internet" as net {
  actor "Global Users" as users
}

users --> cdn : HTTPS
cdn --> lb1 : HTTPS (geo: us-east)
cdn --> lb2 : HTTPS (geo: eu-west)

' Within region 1
lb1 --> appA1 : HTTP
lb1 --> appA2 : HTTP
appA1 --> cache1 : TCP/Redis :6379
appA2 --> cache1 : TCP/Redis :6379
appA1 --> dbPrimary : JDBC :5432 (read/write)
appA2 --> dbPrimary : JDBC :5432 (read/write)

' Within region 2
lb2 --> appB1 : HTTP
lb2 --> appB2 : HTTP
appB1 --> cache2 : TCP/Redis :6379
appB2 --> cache2 : TCP/Redis :6379
' eu-west reads locally from the REPLICA, writes are forwarded upstream
' (read-your-writes consistency handled at the app layer).
appB1 --> dbReplica : JDBC :5432 (local reads)
appB2 --> dbReplica : JDBC :5432 (local reads)

' --- Cross-region replication --------------------------------------------
' This is the key "multi-region" relationship: data flows between regions.
' Label it with the replication protocol and direction.
dbPrimary --> dbReplica : PostgreSQL\nstreaming replication

' --- Control plane wiring -------------------------------------------------
' Both regions report metrics/config to the shared control plane.
' These arrows CROSS frame boundaries — that's intentional and shows
' a dependency that ops must plan for (network egress, latency, blast radius).
appA1 ..> cfg : config pull\n(gRPC)
appB1 ..> cfg : config pull\n(gRPC)
fbA1 ..> metrics : metrics push\n(HTTPS)
fbB1 ..> metrics : metrics push\n(HTTPS)
cicd ..> appA1 : deploy trigger\n(SSH)
cicd ..> appB1 : deploy trigger\n(SSH)

' --- Teaching notes -------------------------------------------------------
note bottom of dbPrimary
  The us-east Postgres is the WRITE primary.
  eu-west is a streaming replica —
  app code must route writes here.
end note

note right of cp
  Control plane is a SHARED
  dependency for BOTH regions.
  If it goes down, deploys and
  config updates stall, but
  serving traffic continues.
end note

' Recap:
'   * TWO regional frames, each self-similar (LB + 2 app + cache + DB).
'   * ONE global CDN edge in front.
'   * ONE shared control plane that spans regions.
'   * Cross-region arrows show replication and control-plane coupling.
'   * Mixed stereotypes: <<device>> for hosts, <<executionEnvironment>> for
'     the OS under HAProxy, <<deploy>> for every artifact.
'   * `..>` (dashed) vs `-->` (solid): dashed for control/async, solid for
'     data/sync traffic — a useful (if informal) convention.

@enduml
